= Appendix J — The Trap File

+ *Arteries are always oxygen-rich?* No: the pulmonary artery carries blood to the lungs.
+ *Tendon joins bones?* No: tendons connect muscle to bone; ligaments connect bones.
+ *All activity is exercise?* No: exercise is planned and structured physical activity.
+ *Warm-up guarantees safety?* No: preparation helps, but it cannot eliminate all risk.
+ *One adjustment suits everyone?* No: ask about the individual's needs and preferences.
+ *Rules never change?* No: use the code and rules specified for the event and date.
+ *Fifteen-second count equals beats per minute?* No: multiply by four for an estimate.
+ *A correct guess proves understanding?* No: explain the reasoning and review uncertainty.


== Selected rules references

Rules change. Check the current competition regulations: #link("https://worldathletics.org/about-iaaf/documents/book-of-rules")[World Athletics], #link("https://www.theifab.com/laws/latest/")[IFAB] and #link("https://www.fivb.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/FIVB-Volleyball_Rules_2021_2024_pe.pdf")[FIVB 2021–2024]. The announced 2027 badminton change is reported by #link("https://www.reuters.com/sports/world-body-approves-switch-3x15-scoring-system-january-2027-2026-04-25/")[Reuters] and #link("http://english.news.cn/20260426/1b4f8a0ad0fc41c6ad59b7eca2c34c2e/c.html")[Xinhua]; check the current BWF rules. These sources do not verify every question or topic in this book.
